    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d497">

                <pb facs="0720" n="710" sameAs="frus:frus1945v03/pg710"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.62114A/4–1145: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harrison</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bern</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-04-11">April 11,
                        1945</date>.<lb/>[Received 5:46 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2132. Foreign Office official just telephones that according to telegram from
                    Swiss Legation Berlin representative that Legation is informed verbally by
                    German Minister Albrecht<anchor n="1" xml:id="d497-f1"/> that German Government
                    would be disposed to leave in camps all POWs<anchor n="2" xml:id="d497-f2"/> as
                    Allies advance provided Allied Governments would obligate themselves not to
                    return to active duty against Germany such POWs. Foreign Office promises written
                        <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> confirming foregoing.</p>
                <p>Repeated to London for Murphy<anchor n="3" xml:id="d497-f3"/> to Paris for <hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">Widewing</hi> B<anchor n="4" xml:id="d497-f4"/> to
                        Spaatz<anchor n="5" xml:id="d497-f5"/> for McDonald<anchor n="6"
                        xml:id="d497-f6"/> attention Bradford and SHAEF for General Barker<anchor
                        n="7" xml:id="d497-f7"/> and to Caserta.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harrison</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d497-f1" n="1" xml:id="d497-f1-content">
                <p>Erich Albrecht, Head of Legal Department of Foreign Ministry.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d497-f2" n="2" xml:id="d497-f2-content">
                <p>Prisoners of War.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d497-f3" n="3" xml:id="d497-f3-content">
                <p>Robert D. Murphy, United States Political Adviser for Germany.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d497-f4" n="4" xml:id="d497-f4-content">
                <p>Military code designation for Supreme Headquarters, Allied Expeditionary
                    Force.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d497-f5" n="5" xml:id="d497-f5-content">
                <p>Gen. Carl Spaatz, Commander of U.S. Strategic Air Forces in Europe.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d497-f6" n="6" xml:id="d497-f6-content">
                <p>Brig. Gen. George C. McDonald, Director of Intelligence, United States Strategic
                    Tactical Air Force, Europe.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d497-f7" n="7" xml:id="d497-f7-content">
                <p>Maj. Gen. Ray W. Barker, Chief of Division of Personnel at Supreme Headquarters,
                    Allied Expeditionary Force, Europe.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
